  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "Nov 2026 releases extend transcriptome resources toward cell-type, isoform and perturbation resolution, with cancer lncRNA and perturbation atlases among them.",
  "synthesis": "The items are mostly database releases that integrate transcriptomic evidence with regulatory, perturbation or genetic-association layers, though they do not all concern cancer. LncRNAfunc 2.0 combines TCGA, GTEx, CCLE, binding and perturbation evidence for cancer lncRNAs, and iGPSC-DB offers an inferred single-cell genetic perturbation atlas. scGWAS-DB links 3,649 GWAS datasets to single-cell atlases covering 74 tissues and 1,713 cell types. Gene Expression Nebulas 2.0 expands standardized expression profiles, and iCellOmics and PlantPAN 5.0 extend multiomics integration to industrial cell lines and plant regulatory networks. A lettuce preprint moves toward isoform-level trait association, identifying trans-sQTL hotspots near LsPPR. The common development is finer-resolution, evidence-integrated annotation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
